#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:1
msgid "Host vs. Device Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:3
msgid ""
"cuTile Rust programs have two parts. Host code runs on the CPU and owns "
"normal Rust control flow, tensor allocation, stream selection, kernel "
"launch, and result readback. Device code runs on the GPU and describes the "
"work performed by each tile block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:5
msgid ""
"use cutile::prelude::*;\n"
"use kernels::scale;\n"
"\n"
"fn main() -> Result<(), cuda_async::error::DeviceError> {\n"
"    let device = cuda_core::Device::new(0)?;\n"
"    let stream = device.new_stream()?;\n"
"\n"
"    let x = api::ones::<f32>(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"    let mut z = api::zeros::<f32>(&[32, 32]).sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"\n"
"    let _ = scale((&mut z).partition([4, 4]), &x, 2.0f32)."
"sync_on(&stream)?;\n"
"    Ok(())\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"#[cutile::module]\n"
"mod kernels {\n"
"    use cutile::core::*;\n"
"\n"
"    #[cutile::entry()]\n"
"    fn scale<const S: [i32; 2]>(\n"
"        z: &mut Tensor<f32, S>,\n"
"        x: &Tensor<f32, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
"        alpha: f32,\n"
"    ) {\n"
"        let tile_x = x.load_like(z);\n"
"        z.store(tile_x * alpha);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:36
msgid ""
"`main` is host code. It constructs tensors, partitions the writable output, "
"and synchronizes the returned `DeviceOp`. `scale` is device code. It runs "
"once per tile block and sees one mutable output partition at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:38
msgid "Modules and Entry Points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:40
msgid ""
"`#[cutile::module]` marks a Rust module whose functions can be compiled for "
"the GPU. `#[cutile::entry()]` marks a function as a kernel entry point. "
"Entry points are callable from host code through generated launcher APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:42
msgid "Entry points follow four rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:44
msgid "They must be inside a `#[cutile::module]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:45
msgid ""
"Writable tensor parameters use static tile shapes, such as `Tensor<f32, S>` "
"or `Tensor<f32, { [BM, BN] }>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:46
msgid ""
"Read-only tensor parameters may use dynamic dimensions, such as `Tensor<f32, "
"{ [-1, -1] }>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:47
msgid ""
"Kernels write results into tensor parameters instead of returning values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/host-vs-device.md:49
msgid ""
"Unmarked functions inside a `#[cutile::module]` are device functions. They "
"can be called from entry points or other device functions and are inlined "
"during compilation, but they cannot be launched directly."
msgstr ""

